            {
                "entry_id": "fe5bf07c-a401-3059-9a86-c7fb6a315386",
                "word": "Bhoutan",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "5a8f548c-bb2c-4238-85a3-9c2130fb47b5",
                        "entry_id": "fe5bf07c-a401-3059-9a86-c7fb6a315386",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "Boutan"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "32bbde5f-bc04-3dfb-b47e-6fe32aa83436",
                        "entry_id": "fe5bf07c-a401-3059-9a86-c7fb6a315386",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Pays d’Asie, entouré par la Chine (Tibet) au nord et l’Inde au sud, dont la capitale est Thimphou et la langue officielle le dzongkha."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Pays"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "53cf06ab-98e4-45de-81f2-234c79de57e8",
                                "sense_id": "32bbde5f-bc04-3dfb-b47e-6fe32aa83436",
                                "text": "Les trois grandes chaînes de la Haute-Asie ressemblent à l’Océan ; elles séparent des races d’hommes et de grandes religions. L’Himalaya entier, moins le Bhoutan, le Sikhim et le Cachemir, est habité par des Hindous qui, nous devons le dire, ne se sont pas conservés aussi purs de tout mélange que leurs frères des diverses castes dans l’Inde propre."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c0163645-6c60-430c-baa8-5632c407144f",
                                "sense_id": "32bbde5f-bc04-3dfb-b47e-6fe32aa83436",
                                "text": "Le Thibet oriental, le Bhoutan, situé dans la portion orientale de l’Himalaya, le Turkestan de Kachgard, et les provinces qui s’étendent à l’est de cette dernière contrée appartiennent à la Chine, qui a su jusqu’à présent soustraire tous ces pays à l’influence de l’Europe, au grand dommage de la géographie et de bien d’autres choses. Heureusement nous avons l’espoir fondé que l’Angleterre, et surtout la Russie, ne tarderont pas à nous ouvrir toutes ces régions."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f7d4687b-3012-4ba1-978d-b08199e86286",
                                "sense_id": "32bbde5f-bc04-3dfb-b47e-6fe32aa83436",
                                "text": "Depuis le commencent de ce siècle plusieurs voyages ont été entrepris à Bhoutan, Sikkim et les districts occidentaux qui avoisinent les possessions anglaises."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "72aafabe-aa5c-45b1-8447-40fb00ca50d5",
                        "source_entry_id": "fe5bf07c-a401-3059-9a86-c7fb6a315386",
                        "source_sense_id": "32bbde5f-bc04-3dfb-b47e-6fe32aa83436",
                        "target_lang_word": "Bhutan",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Bhutan",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "11beb68e-26fb-3ec1-8241-ebc466b46755",
                                        "entry_id": "e1b401b4-e2b7-3ae7-aa61-01a90bb6ce0b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "asiatisches Land im Himalaya"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7a076aa9-ede0-414f-a89f-d72b3bc006fe",
                                                "sense_id": "11beb68e-26fb-3ec1-8241-ebc466b46755",
                                                "text": "Bhutan ist buddhistisch geprägt."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95bcb3ff-03dd-4204-b012-6e947f0a2d2f",
                                                "sense_id": "11beb68e-26fb-3ec1-8241-ebc466b46755",
                                                "text": "Thimphu ist die Hauptstadt von Bhutan."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b4b14e40-5675-41d2-bfd9-e1258653b914",
                                                "sense_id": "11beb68e-26fb-3ec1-8241-ebc466b46755",
                                                "text": "Der Himalaya bestimmt die Landschaft Bhutans."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb1ba405-63ba-4fa9-ad72-79039d8b7d66",
                                                "sense_id": "11beb68e-26fb-3ec1-8241-ebc466b46755",
                                                "text": "Berge über 6000 m Höhe dürfen in Bhutan nicht bestiegen werden, weil die Berggipfel als Wohnstatt von Geistern und Göttern gelten."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1e5a5367-7b42-406a-8ec3-7e34258dd9f5",
                                                "sense_id": "11beb68e-26fb-3ec1-8241-ebc466b46755",
                                                "text": "„Er hatte sieben Jahre lang in der Hauptstadt Tibets und in den Zentren des Buddhismus in Bhutan und Nepal studiert.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "17ca3431-66a2-4170-8005-c644fb091af3",
                        "source_entry_id": "fe5bf07c-a401-3059-9a86-c7fb6a315386",
                        "source_sense_id": "32bbde5f-bc04-3dfb-b47e-6fe32aa83436",
                        "target_lang_word": "Bhutan",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Bhutan",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bcf5a919-ca76-3eeb-87bd-4541e079dcc0",
                                        "entry_id": "905b5be9-c516-3dd9-86fa-31ed81f4766f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A country in South Asia, in the Himalayas. Official name: Kingdom of Bhutan. Capital: Thimphu."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af22b88b-ecc1-4ceb-8a12-6d0797cc5f64",
                                                "sense_id": "bcf5a919-ca76-3eeb-87bd-4541e079dcc0",
                                                "text": "INDIA BEYOND THE GANGES, is a country bounded by Thibet and Boutan on the north ; by China, Tonquin, and Cochin China on the eaſt ; by the Indian Ocean on the ſouth ; and by the hither India , the bay of Bengal, and the Straits of Malacca on the weſt:[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "521d78ae-0249-48f4-a3a4-e93049d1c01c",
                                                "sense_id": "bcf5a919-ca76-3eeb-87bd-4541e079dcc0",
                                                "text": "The problems for Bhutan, a country largely dependent on tourism but that has imposed restrictions to prevent environmental destruction, began worsening since the coronavirus pandemic.\nThe mountainous and isolated kingdom has opted in recent years for a timid openness but remains firm in its desire to avoid mass tourism and to preserve an identity shaped, compared to other minorities, around the traditions of the Tibetan-origin ‘Drukpa’ ethnic group, which professes Mahayana Buddhism."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c88aab61-91b6-471a-bf2e-b49151d001c6",
                                                "sense_id": "bcf5a919-ca76-3eeb-87bd-4541e079dcc0",
                                                "text": "Most foreigners who have heard of Bhutan know two things: the country charges international visitors a $100/day sustainable development fee (aka tourist tax), and that it is the birthplace of the Gross National Happiness Index, a system intended to look after the well-being of citizens and the environment."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
